      "name": "Winchester Transload Operations",
      "description": "Winchester transload operations: the Winchester-branch execution of a single transload job, from appointment to empty return. The appointment is booked before the container leaves the terminal. At the branch the container is devanned and destuffed; the freight is counted, inspected, and photographed, with exceptions reported in writing the same day; reworked as the job requires — palletized, wrapped, labeled, sorted by destination, purchase order, or SKU; restacked into 53ft domestic trailers (a 40ft container fills about 20 pallet positions, a 20ft about 10); dispatched inland the same day or the next morning; the empty container returned immediately after devanning, before per-diem accrues; and the final mile run by appointment. Domain reference, labeled as such: devanning happens at a warehouse or container freight station; floor-loaded and palletized are the two handling modes; cross-dock dwell is measured in hours, storage between legs in days. Every container transloading job is quoted per job and agreed in writing before dispatch — the only pricing basis published for this service. Not published and not claimed: any named port terminal or ramp; any drayage performer or chassis source; any list of handled container types.",
